  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> are isoelectronic ionic species. For monatomic ionic isoelectronic species as positive charge increases ionic size decreases.</p><p>The order of size of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#38;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Increasing order of ionic radii:&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p>"
